WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:13.942
<v Narrator>Welcome to Once Upon a Time Show. It's time for a bedtime story. Hello, little one. Pull your blanket up to your chin, nice and warm.

2
00:00:14.242 --> 00:00:22.644
<v Narrator>Tonight's story is a very old one. It's one of Aesop's fables, from a book called The Aesop for Children. We tell it in our own words.

3
00:00:22.944 --> 00:00:29.722
<v Narrator>It's about a family of busy little ants, and a grasshopper who loved music. Are you ready? Let's listen.

4
00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:35.568
<v Narrator>Once upon a time, in a big sunny meadow, there lived a happy green grasshopper.

5
00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:46.322
<v Narrator>He had long legs, bright eyes, and a tiny fiddle that he carried everywhere. In the morning he played, and in the evening he played some more. Zing, zing, zing!

6
00:00:46.622 --> 00:00:54.165
<v Narrator>The flowers swayed to his music. The butterflies danced. And the grasshopper sang, la la la, all summer long.

7
00:00:54.465 --> 00:01:01.161
<v Narrator>Why should I worry? he said. The sun is warm, the grass is green, and there's plenty to eat.

8
00:01:07.461 --> 00:01:13.359
<v Narrator>Not far away lived a family of ants. They were small and brown, and they were always busy.

9
00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:22.797
<v Narrator>Every day they marched in a long line, one, two, one, two. They carried seeds and grains of wheat to their home under the ground.

10
00:01:23.097 --> 00:01:31.716
<v Narrator>Come and play with me! called the grasshopper. But the ants shook their heads. We're saving food for the winter, they said, and on they marched.

11
00:01:32.016 --> 00:01:38.584
<v Narrator>The grasshopper laughed and played another tune. Winter is far, far away, he thought.

12
00:01:45.884 --> 00:01:54.368
<v Narrator>Then, little by little, the days grew shorter. The leaves turned orange and gold, and a cool wind blew across the meadow.

13
00:01:54.668 --> 00:02:01.843
<v Narrator>One bright autumn morning, the ants were busy in the warm sunshine, drying the grain they had saved all summer.

14
00:02:02.143 --> 00:02:11.904
<v Narrator>Along came the grasshopper, with his fiddle under his arm. His tummy was rumbling. Please, he asked softly, could you spare me a little something to eat?

15
00:02:12.204 --> 00:02:23.727
<v Narrator>The ants were surprised. Didn't you save any food for the winter? they asked. What were you doing all summer long? I was so busy with my music, said the grasshopper, that the summer slipped away.

16
00:02:24.027 --> 00:02:31.408
<v Narrator>Music, was it? said the ants. Well then, perhaps now it's time for dancing! And they went back to their work.

17
00:02:37.708 --> 00:02:47.132
<v Narrator>The grasshopper sat down on a stone and thought for a long while. The ants are right, he said quietly. There's a time for work, and a time for play.

18
00:02:47.432 --> 00:02:55.614
<v Narrator>So he hopped off to find the last seeds hiding in the grass. And he found a snug little hollow under a fallen leaf, out of the wind.

19
00:02:55.914 --> 00:03:03.969
<v Narrator>And he made himself a promise. Next summer, I'll gather food in the morning, he said. And when the work is done, I'll play my fiddle.

20
00:03:11.269 --> 00:03:20.600
<v Narrator>And now the meadow is quiet. The ants are asleep in their cozy home. And the grasshopper is tucked under his leaf, humming a soft little tune.

21
00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:26.528
<v Narrator>Work a little, play a little, and rest when the night comes. Just like you, little one.

22
00:03:26.828 --> 00:03:35.347
<v Narrator>Close your eyes now. Breathe in, breathe out, nice and slow. Goodnight from Once Upon a Time Show. Sweet dreams.
